--- !u!114 &1384491896
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1384491894}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Well, classes just started a few days ago and I'm\u2026 not sure how I
    feel about them. Some classes seem really exciting and I can't wait to start,
    but others just feel\u2026 dull? I don't know, maybe I'll just have to wait and
    see. The source material is super interesting though, especially Anthropology
    2, it's just some of the teachers that have me a little worried\u2026 They have
    no real passion or anything\u2014you can tell pretty easily\u2014and those kind
    of teachers are the worst.\n\n\nMy other roommate is pretty nice. Her name is
    Sofia, and she seems pretty introverted, so we haven't talked much. The few 19nteractions
    we've had so far have been friendly though, so I'm hoping she'll warm up to us.\n\n\nCollege
    life has been interesting for sure. Part of me misses home and wishes I were
    still living close to my high school friends (its only an hour or so drive, so
    19 can go back if I really wanted, but at the same time, it's still a big time
    commitment when so much has been going on) but another part of me really likes
    it here. At least I don't have to wake up at six in the morning to carpool to
    school anymore, so pros and cons :P\n\n\nThe people have been\u2026 fine??? There
    are a lot of different people here, which makes seeing different perspectives
    so interesting! But\u2026 there are some people here who I feel would call me
    a slur without missing a beat 10f I interacted with them too much. I try to avoid
    them whenever possible, but it's just a bit rough :[\n\n\nI do think I am going
    to get along with the people in my classes, just based off the way they've been
    acting so far, but 16t's still a bit too early to see so far. I'm hoping to make
    some friends, especially so that I can have someone to work with on group projects.\n\n\nSpeaking
    of friends, I think something might be wrong with Ethan. He hasn't been responding
    to any of my messages in weeks, which is completely unlike him, but no one else
    seems to even notice. Also, I heard from one of our mutual friends that he was
    apparently supposed to room in the same building as Regan and I, but there's
    been no word for a while. Maybe I should see if his sister knows anything.\n\n\nI
    would write more, but 15 have homework to focus on for now\u2026\n\n\nI'21 definitely
    try to write some more when I get the time, wouldn't want to make things harder
    on a future historian would we ;}\n\n(Regan is looking over my shoulder as I
    write this, they're always so mean to me T^T (lighthearted))\n\n\nCasey Wakefield,
    signing off :}\n\n\n\n\n\nIt's been a couple hours since I wrote this and something
    feels off. I swear I wrote more but when I look back, there's nothing there beyond
    the spacing that I normally put around paragraphs. I don't know what's going
    on, but maybe it just didn't save? But then why are the paragraph20 after it
    perfectly fine? I have the worst luck with technology. I'll have to see if there's
    something on this computer or the internet that could explain things. It's got
    to be some kind of bug. That's the only thing that would make sense. I really
    don't want to have to get a new computer again :'{"
